{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791630714,"nonce":"wLh1rDCKUXHPL4yWOOLEBGV1B7w=","title":"What motion costs, and keeping it small","message":"benchmarks/motion.mjs (release addon; Apple M1 Pro, Node 24.2, 2026-10-10; 2000 elements offscreen, 300 in a 2x window at 120 Hz). Medians of three runs on a normally loaded machine; the machine was later loaded by other jobs (load average 25-80) and runs then are discarded.\n\nOffscreen, per frame while running, 2000 elements:\n- paint transitions (two properties each): ~1.5 ms, ~0.8 us per element\n- keyframe animations (two properties): ~1.8 ms\n- layout transitions (width) including relayout: ~3.0-3.4 ms, against ~0.2 ms for one plain layout\n- FLIP moves: ~0.8-0.9 ms; starting them after an insert: ~1.6-2.0 ms\n- starting 4000 transitions on a class change: ~15-20 ms, against ~9-12 ms applying the change at once\n\nRestyle overhead of declaring transitions (a theme variable change restyling all 2000): plain ~8 ms against ~12.5 ms (+55%) with every element parsing its declaration each restyle. Caching parsed declarations by text brought it to ~+33% (0f4df81); sharing them by Arc was measured only under heavy load, to be re-measured.\n\nMemory: an element with a transition declared keeps ~1.5 KB of motion state (NodeMotion 192 B, a parsed spec ~230 B shared once cached, base and shown maps of 112 B writes); each property in flight adds a 328 B run. Six on/off cycles of 2000 elements: RSS flat, no growth.\n\nWindow, 300 boxes animating continuously: 28-31% of a core at 119 fps, of which the motion tick is 4.5-4.8% (0.38-0.41 ms a frame); the rest is drawing a frame every 8 ms. Paused: 0.1-0.3% CPU, 0 fps. RSS 12-17 MB higher while animating than still.\n\nOpen: culling motion out of view (as ashui does with tree.inView), so off-screen animation asks for no frames; then re-measure the restyle overhead and the window out of view.","files":null}]}